rust-camel is an independent reimplementation, in Rust, of the integration model of
Apache Camel (https://camel.apache.org/, https://github.com/apache/camel): its routes,
Enterprise Integration Patterns, component and endpoint names, options, headers and the
Simple language. It is written from scratch and contains no Apache Camel source code.
Apache Camel, Camel and Apache are trademarks of The Apache Software Foundation. rust-camel
is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by The Apache Software Foundation.

This product bundles:

- The IANA Time Zone Database (https://www.iana.org/time-zones), release 2026f, compiled
  into crates/camel-core/tzdata/zones.bin from the PyPI "tzdata" package. The time zone
  database is in the public domain.

- Test images from the ZXing project's blackbox test suite (https://github.com/zxing/zxing),
  Copyright ZXing authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, in
  crates/camel-dataformats/src/barcode/testdata/zxing (see ATTRIBUTION.txt there).

The benchmark harness in benchmarks/java-camel depends on Apache Camel and other Java
libraries, downloaded by Maven at build time and not redistributed here.
